bitcoin-core for DWDC
=====================

This is a DWDC build. It is NOT an upstream Bitcoin Core release.

Upstream did not build it, did not sign it, and is not responsible for
it. It is built from the upstream release tag by DWDC, signed with the
DWDC APT key, and it carries the patch listed below. Report problems
with this package to DWDC, not to the Bitcoin Core project.

Source
------

Upstream tag:  v31.1
Packaging:     DarkWebDivingClub/bitcoin-core, branch
               packaging/ubuntu/resolute
Patch branch:  dwdc/signet-blocktime

Everything outside debian/ and the patch below is the upstream tag,
unmodified. You can verify that:

    git clone https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin
    git -C bitcoin diff v31.1 <this-source> -- . ':(exclude)debian'

Patches applied
---------------

1. "Allow configuring target block time for a signet"
   Author:  benthecarman <benthecarman@live.com>
   Origin:  https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27446
            (proposed to Bitcoin Core, closed unmerged 2024-01-10)
            Carried by Bitcoin Knots as d8434da3c1.
   Size:    4 files, 12 insertions, 1 deletion.

   Adds -signetblocktime, so a custom signet can target a block time
   other than ten minutes. Without it, a signet mined faster raises its
   own difficulty every 2016 blocks until it drifts back to ten-minute
   blocks, because the target spacing is compiled into SigNetParams.

   Scope: signet only. Every line it changes is inside SigNetParams,
   behind a std::optional that stays empty unless -signetblocktime is
   passed, which itself requires -signetchallenge. Mainnet, testnet and
   regtest use separate parameter classes and are untouched. Verified:
   stock and patched bitcoind produce identical genesis hashes on
   mainnet, the default signet, and regtest, and the only difference in
   the whole option list is the new -signetblocktime entry.

   Consequence: this build can follow custom signets that stock Bitcoin
   Core cannot. The reverse is the problem worth knowing about -- a
   stock node pointed at such a chain does not error, it forks.

   contrib/signet/miner additionally gains --block-interval, since it
   otherwise paces at ten minutes regardless of what the chain targets.
   That script is not shipped in this package.

What the signature attests
--------------------------

That DWDC built this package from the upstream tag named above plus the
patch named above. It is not a reproducible build. It does not attest
that these binaries match those published by the Bitcoin Core project --
they do not, because of the patch.

 -- DWDC <apt@dwdc.club>
